1. Problem Statement
College students struggle to manage multiple assignments, deadlines, and study sessions across different courses, 
leading to missed deadlines and increased academic stress. Existing task management apps are either too complex for
quick task entry or lack features tailored to academic workflows. StudyMate addresses this by providing a simple, 
student-focused task manager that organizes assignments by course, tracks deadlines, and sends timely reminders—helping
students stay on top of their academic responsibilities without overwhelming them with unnecessary features.

2. User Research (Simulated)
Participants Profile
Sarah, 19 - Freshman, Biology major, uses phone for everything, struggles with paper planners
Marcus, 21 - Junior, Computer Science, currently uses sticky notes and Google Calendar
Priya, 20 - Sophomore, Business, juggles 5 courses + part-time job
Chen, 22 - Senior, Engineering, needs visual deadline tracking
Aaliyah, 18 - Freshman, English major, new to college workload management
Jake, 20 - Sophomore, History, forgets to check planner apps regularly
Emma, 21 - Junior, Psychology, wants course-specific organization
David, 19 - Freshman, Math major, overwhelmed by multiple assignment types
Key Insights
Insight 1: Students want to add tasks in under 30 seconds—long forms cause app abandonment
Insight 2: 7 out of 8 participants organize tasks by course/class rather than by date alone
Insight 3: Visual deadline indicators (color-coding for urgency) are preferred over just dates
Insight 4: Students check their phones 50+ times daily—micro-interactions matter more than desktop sync
Insight 5: Push notifications are essential, but students want granular control (per-course settings)
