4. User Flow: Adding a New Task
Start: User opens StudyMate app

Step 1: User sees Home screen with existing tasks and prominent "+" button

Step 2: User taps "+" button

Step 3: Add Task screen appears with minimal form fields

Step 4: User enters task title (e.g., "Essay draft")

Step 5: User selects course from dropdown (e.g., "English 202")

Step 6: User picks due date using date picker

Step 7: (Optional) User adds brief notes or selects priority level

Step 8: User taps "Save Task" button

Step 9: System validates input and saves task

Step 10: Confirmation appears (brief animation or checkmark)

Step 11: User returns to Home screen where new task is visible in list

End: User sees updated task list, feels confident task is saved

Alternative Flow: User taps "Cancel" at Step 8 → Returns to Home without saving

