6. Figma Design Instructions (Step-by-Step)
Getting Started in Figma
Step 1: Set Up Your File

Open Figma and create new file: "StudyMate Wireframes"
Click "Frame" tool (shortcut: F) in top toolbar
Select "Phone" category from right panel
Choose "iPhone 14 Pro" or "Android Large" (390 x 844 px is common)
Create 6 frames total, one for each screen
Name each frame clearly: "1-Splash", "2-Home", "3-AddTask", "4-Confirmation", "5-EditTask", "6-Settings"
Step 2: Set Up Your Color Palette

Create a small "Style Guide" frame to the left
Add three rectangles:
White (#FFFFFF) - backgrounds
Light Grey (#E5E5E5) - borders, inactive elements
Dark Grey (#333333) - text, active buttons
Save these as color styles: Right-click rectangle → Create Style → name it
Step 3: Basic Tools You'll Use

Rectangle Tool (R):

Use for buttons, input fields, cards, containers
Draw rectangle → adjust corner radius in right panel (0–10px for sharp to slightly rounded)
Text Tool (T):

Click to add text
Set font to system default (Inter, Roboto, or Arial)
Font sizes: 24px (headings), 16px (body), 14px (labels), 12px (subtext)
Line Tool (L):

Create dividers and borders
Set stroke weight: 1px for subtle lines, 2px for emphasis
Ellipse Tool (O):

Use for circular buttons, icons, radio buttons
Hold Shift while dragging to create perfect circles
Step 4: Build Screen 1 (Splash/Login)

Select "1-Splash" frame
Add app name:
Press T, click in upper-center area
Type "StudyMate", set to 32px, bold, dark grey
Add tagline:
Below app name, 16px, regular weight, medium grey
Type "Your academic task companion"
Add icon placeholder:
Press O, draw 80x80px circle above app name
Add border, no fill
Inside circle: Draw simple shapes (book or checkmark) using Rectangle/Line tools
Add buttons at bottom:
Press R, draw rectangle (300px wide, 48px tall)
Center horizontally
Add text: "Login" centered in button
Duplicate (Cmd/Ctrl + D), move below
Change text to "Sign Up", fill with dark grey
Add version text at very bottom (12px, light grey)
Step 5: Build Screen 2 (Home)

